.TH SWISSARMY\-USB 1 2026-11-05 swissarmy\-usb "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swissarmy\-usb \- build a multiboot USB stick with Ventoy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swissarmy\-usb
.RB [ \-n ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.RI [ options ]
.PP
.B ./setup.sh
.RB [ \-n ]
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B swissarmy\-usb
sets up a Ventoy multiboot USB stick on Ubuntu: it installs the vendored
Ventoy release, copies three GRUB themes, downloads and verifies the ISOs
listed in
.I isos.conf
(installers, disk tools, rescue systems, security distros and offline
antivirus), and generates Ventoy's configuration.
.PP
It is
.I setup.sh
from the swissarmy\-usb repository, usually linked into
.I ~/.local/bin
as
.B swissarmy\-usb
by the
.B link
command. Hints in its output use the name it was run as.
.PP
Where a command takes
.RI [ mount | device ],
pass the stick's mountpoint, its device (mounted with
.BR udisksctl (1)
if needed), or nothing: a mounted stick labelled
.B SWISSARMY
or
.B Ventoy
is found automatically.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR deps " [" \-\-qemu ]
Install the required tools with
.BR apt\-get :
git, curl, jq, gnupg, aria2, pv, exfatprogs, dosfstools, parted, xz\-utils,
udisks2 and util\-linux.
.B \-\-qemu
adds qemu\-system\-x86 and ovmf for the
.B test
command.
.TP
.BI install " device"
Install Ventoy with GPT and Secure Boot support on
.IR device .
.B This erases the whole device.
See
.BR SAFETY .
.TP
.BI update " device"
Update Ventoy on an existing stick to the vendored version.
ISOs and configuration are kept.
.TP
.BR themes " [" \fImount\fR | \fIdevice\fR ]
Copy the Catppuccin Mocha, Tokyo Night and Vimix GRUB themes to
.IR ventoy/theme/ ,
then regenerate the configuration.
.TP
.BR isos " [" \fImount\fR | \fIdevice\fR "] [" \fIid\fR ...]
Download, verify and place the ISOs from
.IR isos.conf :
all of them, or only the given ids.
An id prefix selects every id that starts with it
.RB ( kali
is kali\-netinst and kali\-live).
ISOs already up to date are skipped and interrupted downloads resume.
Each download is checked against its SHA256 and, where the project signs its
releases, a GPG signature from a pinned key fingerprint; anything that fails
is deleted and reported.
Windows 10/11 and Redo Rescue can't be downloaded and are copied from
.BR \-\-from .
Exits non\-zero if any ISO failed.
.TP
.BR config " [" \fImount\fR | \fIdevice\fR ]
Regenerate
.I ventoy/ventoy.json
(themes, menu aliases, tips, persistence) and
.I Files/isos.md
on the stick.
.BR themes ,
.B isos
and
.B persistence
do this by themselves.
.TP
.BI persistence " name" " \fR[\fImount\fR|\fIdevice\fR] [" \-\-size " MB\fR]"
Create the persistence image
.IR ventoy/persistence/name .dat
for the ISO
.I name
(an id, or a prefix such as
.BR kali ).
Only entries with a
.B persistence
key in
.I isos.conf
support it.
.TP
.BR test " \fIdevice\fR|\fIimage\fR [" \-\-uefi ]
Boot the stick or a disk image in QEMU, with BIOS or, with
.BR \-\-uefi ,
OVMF.
.TP
.BI all " device"
Everything in order:
.BR deps ,
.BR install ,
label the data partition
.BR SWISSARMY ,
.BR themes ,
.B isos
and
.BR config .
.TP
.BI ventoy\-bump " version"
Download a Ventoy Linux release, check it against the release's
.IR sha256.txt ,
and vendor it in
.I ventoy/
of the clone.
.TP
.B link
Make
.B swissarmy\-usb
a command: symlink
.I setup.sh
into
.IR ~/.local/bin ,
this man page into
.I ~/.local/share/man/man1
and the bash completion into
.IR ~/.local/share/bash\-completion/completions .
Existing files that aren't links to the clone are left alone.
.TP
.B unlink
Remove the symlinks created by
.BR link .
.TP
.B help
Show the usage summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print what would be done and change nothing.
Resolving versions and checking signatures still runs, since it only reads.
.TP
.BI \-\-from " dir"
Copy the manual ISOs (Windows 10/11, Redo Rescue) from
.IR dir .
The newest file matching the entry's
.B match
pattern is used.
.TP
.B \-\-replace
With
.BR isos :
replace manual ISOs already on the stick with the newest matching file in
.BR \-\-from .
Only for manual ISOs, and only for the ids given.
The old ISO is replaced once the copy is complete.
.TP
.BI \-\-size " MB"
Size of the persistence image (default 4096, at least 64).
.TP
.B \-\-uefi
With
.BR test :
boot with OVMF (UEFI) instead of BIOS.
.TP
.B \-\-qemu
With
.BR deps :
also install qemu\-system\-x86 and ovmf.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the usage summary.
.SH SAFETY
.B install
and
.B all
erase the target, so they only accept whole disks that are removable or on
USB, refuse a disk with a system mount
.RI ( / ,
.IR /boot ,
.IR /home ,
swap, ...) or a filesystem mounted outside
.IR /media ,
.I /run/media
or
.IR /mnt ,
refuse the disk holding
.IR / ,
show the disk with
.BR lsblk (8)
and require its name to be typed.
There is no option to skip that confirmation.
.PP
The other commands only write to a Ventoy stick: the target's disk must have
Ventoy's
.B VTOYEFI
partition.
.B isos
locks the stick, so two runs can't download onto it at once.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWISSARMY_ALLOW_LOOP
Set to 1 to accept loop devices, for testing with
.BR losetup (8).
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Torrent downloads (Kali Live) go to
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/swissarmy\-usb
(default
.IR ~/.cache/swissarmy\-usb )
when the PC has room, and are then copied to the stick.
.SH FILES
In the clone:
.TP
.I isos.conf
The ISO manifest: folders, ISOs, download sources, verification, pins.
.TP
.I config/ventoy.tmpl.json
Template for
.IR ventoy.json :
theme settings, resolution, menu options.
.TP
.I ventoy/VERSION
The vendored Ventoy version, its checksum and where its source is.
.PP
On the stick:
.TP
.I ventoy/ventoy.json
The generated Ventoy configuration.
.TP
.I Files/isos.md
The list of ISOs: version, language, date, source and SHA256.
.TP
.I Files/.swissarmy/
Download state and partial downloads.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; non\-zero when a command fails, including when any ISO fails to
download or verify.
.SH EXAMPLES
Preview, then build a stick on
.IR /dev/sdb :
.PP
.nf
.RS
swissarmy\-usb \-\-dry\-run all /dev/sdb
swissarmy\-usb all /dev/sdb
.RE
.fi
.PP
Update the ISOs, and add the manual ones from the Downloads folder:
.PP
.nf
.RS
swissarmy\-usb isos
swissarmy\-usb isos \-\-from ~/Downloads windows redorescue
.RE
.fi
.PP
Show what is outdated without downloading anything:
.PP
.nf
.RS
swissarmy\-usb \-n isos
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lsblk (8),
.BR udisksctl (1),
.BR qemu\-system\-x86_64 (1)
.PP
